        "original_id": "987be0f0-30d5-5140-9de3-7873c3f8655a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: August Wilson, Robert Gossett, Russell Taylor\n- Works: Fences, The Pittsburgh Cycle, The Closer, A Raisin in the Sun, The Last Minstrel Show\n- Roles: American playwright, fictional character, Assistant Chief\n\nFacts:\n- August Wilson was born on April 27, 1945, and he became an American playwright.\n- August Wilson created a series of ten plays called The Pittsburgh Cycle and received two Pulitzer Prizes for Drama for his work.\n- Fences is a 1985 play by American playwright August Wilson.\n- Robert Gossett acted in the Broadway production of Lloyd Richards's Fences, Hal Scott's A Raisin in the Sun, and Donald McKayle's The Last Minstrel Show.\n- August Wilson died on October 2, 2005.\n- Russell Taylor is a fictional Assistant Chief character in TNT's The Closer, and Robert Gossett portrayed him.",
